    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded around 1336 by the Sangama brothers on the Tungabhadra as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> power collapsed in the south.</li><li>Under Krishnadevaraya (r. 1509–1529) it was the dominant power of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#india">India</a>, ruled from a vast capital at Hampi.</li><li>Defeat at Talikota in 1565 led to the sack of the capital; nayaka governors became independent and the empire ended by 1646.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The site of Madras, where the English built Fort St George in 1639–40, was granted by a local nayaka who served the Aravidu kings of Vijayanagara.</p></aside>
    </section>

